{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/555337-beast-the-usual","id":555337,"title":"[Beast]The Usual","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-14T23:19:46-07:00","id":555337,"title":"[Beast]The Usual","content":"Just something I wrote up last semester<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Gwyneth didn\u2019t understand people who bought 2% milk. She was fairly sure that\u2019s what caused people to become abusive.<br /> <br /> The Anderson\u2019s apartment, fourth floor of six with a magnificent window view of the alley, had been to Gwyneth\u2019s liking up until she had found the milk in their refrigerator. The housing complex was within the slum reformation project, and the Andersons weren\u2019t abundantly wealthy, but their apartment was neatly furnished with nice upholstery and tables, all modern design with touches of the old excess of the 50\u2019s glamour era bought on budget, and furthermore it was arranged with a designer\u2019s eye, all arranged to please the eye without drawing attention. It was an attempt to hold onto class and dignity when one was losing their hold on it, which Gwyneth approved of. Elegance in the face of despair was the truest form of defiance. As such, when she entered through the window a few minutes ago, she had tried to maintain the integrity of it by shaking the pouring rain off of herself before going into the rest of the apartment. It hadn\u2019t done much good, but she didn\u2019t want to mess up the place.<br /> <br /> The kitchen was sparsely stocked, and most of the products were chosen for their economy rather than taste, but still Gwyneth found an excellent chai tea in the cupboards. The Andersons, or maybe Margaret alone she hoped, believed in having a small taste of good stuff in all circumstances, refusing to go into fortune\u2019s reversal quietly. Gwyneth started making herself a cup exactly the way she liked it, and that was when she found the milk.<br /> <br /> This, she was convinced, was Lawrence\u2019s fault. The man hadn\u2019t taken well to losing his job, his house, his car, his ideal to the court case with his daughter. When they moved under Gwyneth\u2019s watch, he was surly enough, and when her Loving Network told her that they\u2019d been hearing and seeing worrying signs, Gwyneth almost didn\u2019t bother watching for a week to confirm details. The man didn\u2019t have anyone to blame, or at least anyone who he could act against, so he turned to what he had. What Gwyneth\u2019s didn\u2019t understand, looking at the milk in the fridge, was whether the milk was additional punishment from an irrationally abusive man, or if that was the very reason the man was always going to be irrational. Heaven forbid she\u2019d go crazy if she spent her time drinking nasty water mixed with the barest hint of true delight. Full milk or nothing, that\u2019s what makes for a sane mind.<br /> <br /> Gwyneth sighed and finished making her cup of chai tea, trying not to think about how much lesser it was with the crappy milk. While good chai was her addiction, the point was not delicacy, but presentation, and it would do for now. She went back to the living room, and picked out a seat in a darker corner of the room to sit in, dragged it further into the corner and skewing it. She would be readily apparent in place due to the careful placement of the room, but not in form due to the dark. It was a classic overlord position, menacing and secretive and violating. She thought about going through their clothes and finding something nice to wear to take it further-well, truth be told she also would have liked wearing nicer clothes for these kind of things anyways- but decided her raggedy look added a touch of violence to the presentation that she couldn\u2019t otherwise provide. With nothing else to do, Gwyneth sat down in the seat and tried to get her face and posture to fit her image of domination, while sipping slowly at her tea.<br /> <br /> Lawrence Anderson walked in about twelve minutes later, holding a soaking coat with water dripping from his short brown hair into his stormy grey eyes. He actually managed to walk halfway to the kitchen before he noticed anything wrong, which screwed up the angle Gwyneth was going for as he turned to face her, dropping shades from cold pale to haunted pale.<br /> <br /> She took a quick sip, wishing the tea were warmer. \u201cHands where I can see them, Lawrence. This conversation could go bad for you if you decide to text the cops.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did you do to me, earlier today? What are you doing in my house?! GET OUT!\u201d Lawrence sputtered, hands shaking at his sides, eyes fully locked onto the intruder in his house.<br /> <br /> Gwyneth blew on her already too chill cup and looked Lawrence back in the eyes, boring soul-deep into them. \u201cLet\u2019s try again. Keep your hands at the level of your eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lawrence brought up his hands in frustration, about to yell, but found his words caught with his arms. His frustration was building like a steam engine, but he didn\u2019t have it in him to flail his arms, and with that his words were locked up. The need to move, the need to swing, it was all bound to a need to directly express, and in that moment he wasn\u2019t sure how to do that.<br /> <br /> So, hands at the level of his eyes, he sputtered as his face turned red, trying to think of what would be good enough to say or do.<br /> <br /> Gwyneth\u2019s took another sip before continuing, unmoved. \u201cWhat I did earlier was simply show you a truth-that everyone knows what you\u2019re doing and that many of them aren\u2019t tolerating it. They wanted to do more, but I held them back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy would you do that?!\u201d Lawrence yelled, shaking his hands at her. \u201cWhat have I ever done to you?! Why would you care?!\u201d Gwyneth watched his hands, smirking at the line they drew.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou live under my watch. There are rules, and there are prices to pay that come with that. I need you to understand the situation you\u2019re in, that you don\u2019t live with the downtrodden, but in a nest of furies ready to tear you apart for hurting others. I need you to understand that so you can appreciate the alternative I\u2019m about to offer you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She had gotten good at this pitch. Most of it was patently untrue- there was no way everyone in the neighborhood could know, let alone everyone in Lawrence\u2019s business, his favorite lunch shop, at the grocery, and pretty much everywhere he went. No, Gwyneth caught his eye earlier and dug up his vain worry, gave it a life of its\u2019 own, and let it terrorize him. The nightmare set the stage for his day, and some select people in her Network and Guard just took extra steps to make sure he really felt persecuted. His living under her watch was true, though-she was making her slice of the world how she wanted it, and abuse wasn\u2019t tolerated here.<br /> <br /> Of course, that wasn\u2019t what moved her. Her soul was stirring now, at the first hints of subjugation. There was a man about to break, and her soul could smell it.<br /> <br /> Lawrence was a predictable man. \u201cFuck you! I can call the cops on you for breaking and entering, and you haven\u2019t got shit! Don\u2019t sit there like you can judge-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cI have video footage of you beating your wife on three different occasions within the past two weeks. One\u2019s sitting around waiting to be delivered by the cops, another to the local gang, and a third to your business. So, no matter what happens, someone\u2019s going to do something if this gets out. Depending on how tonight goes, those will either end up getting into some really bad hands for you, or they could just sit around. As for my problems, you think I\u2019d move like this without some key people in my pocket?\u201d<br /> <br /> Lawrence almost gagged. \u201cYou-you\u2019re blackmailing me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEssentially, yea-yes.\u201d Gwyneth thought that yeah sounded pretty lame, all limp and non-committal. Yes was stronger, more definite. Course, changing her mind mid-word wasn\u2019t cool either. Now, lying about people bailing her on blackmail and breaking and entering, that was cool.<br /> <br /> Lawrence shook in place. Gwyneth could tell he was about to attack, so she looked him in the eye again. \u201cThis isn\u2019t as bad as you think. Make two oaths and you keep walking. Move against me or walk away from this, and your actions will come rip you to shreds.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lawrence kept shaking, and Gwyneth thought she might have to give him another order to keep him from attacking. She wasn\u2019t crazy about that- she preferred people taking things on themselves. But eventually, Lawrence took a steadying breath. \u201cWhat do you mean by oaths?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gwyneth smiled, drained her cup of cold tea, and stood. She was already a tall woman, at six feet two inches, but her soul was even larger still, and in her gluttony her soul was standing and flaring her wings. No one could see this, but they could feel it-she was a giant in any room, pecking away space greedily with her presence and shadow. She approached Lawrence, got right in his personal space, and tilted his face to look up at hers, locking his eyes with hers.<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst, you never hurt Margaret again. You take marriage counseling, read self-help books, move out if you have to, whatever. But you support her as you\u2019re supposed to, and you never hurt her again. If you don\u2019t, I\u2019ll make sure you never hurt anyone again.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Second, you serve me. I need you to pay some bills, you do that. I need you to watch someone, you watch them. If the unlikely happens and I need you to hurt someone, you hurt them. I\u2019ll call on you as reasonably as I can, but when I call, you come. You don\u2019t, and I will find you and make you obey.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen I think you\u2019ve reformed enough to not hurt Margaret, when I think you\u2019ve properly fixed what\u2019s wrong with you, then I will let you go, free to do what you want. But in the mean time, you. Serve. Me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She had him. All she had to do was let reality settle on his ego, and he\u2019d snap. Later on, she\u2019d make clear to Margaret what happened, give her contacts to help report on activities, and see if her gratitude would get her to join the Loving Network. Lawrence would have to be handled carefully with the other indebted folk of Gwyneth\u2019s watch- the Fearful Guard, as she called them, could get the wrong idea grouping together if the wrong individuals talked to one another, so she\u2019d keep him strictly on watch duty for a month or two. But none of that mattered. What mattered to her was that she was doing good with her hunger, and she was about to feed. Her soul reared up and gave a dreadful caw, watching Lawrence at her wings wrapped around his fracturing will.<br /> <br /> She could see his heart break in his eyes, hands level with his eyes like he was beholding what terrible ruler stood on top of the world, as he finally conceded.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I\u2019ll do it. I\u2019ll do what you say.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gwyneth Warren smiled, and ate Lawrence Anderson\u2019s broken pride with her monstrous soul.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T02:34:43-07:00","id":555427,"title":"","content":"Well, that was an awesome bit of fiction.<br /> <br /> Something it made me consider: it would behoove the Begotten that engage in less savory activities to make a Chamber in their Lair a Prison Cell to facilitate escapes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}